# Implement one-command CLI and remote modes

## Goal

Make one installed `protonmail-ai` binary usable directly by a person, as a
local MCP server, or as an explicitly configured remote service.

## Required work

- Implement `auth`, `mail`, `mcp`, and `serve` command groups.
- Keep one application service layer behind CLI, MCP, and remote transports.
- Provide a one-command installation path with integrity verification.
- Define remote authentication, TLS, tenancy, rate limits, and secret storage.
- Keep remote binding disabled unless explicitly configured.

## Acceptance criteria

- One documented command installs the complete product.
- CLI and MCP produce equivalent results for the same accepted operation.
- Remote mode cannot start with unsafe defaults or an accidental public bind.
- Local usage needs no cloud account or hosted intermediary.
- Installation, upgrade, and removal are exercised on claimed platforms.

## Evidence

- End-to-end CLI/MCP equivalence tests
- Remote deployment threat-model extension
- Fresh-machine installation transcript
